WEBVTT

00:16.683 --> 00:18.977
He is someone who is
always helping me. Mr. Sakumoto.

00:19.060 --> 00:22.814
I had heard
that you were a former athlete.

00:23.314 --> 00:25.275
I think that it's amazing how you have

00:25.358 --> 00:27.110
found another path for yourself,

00:27.193 --> 00:30.071
even after ending
your career as an athlete.

00:30.780 --> 00:32.782
It's not something that everyone can do.

00:45.253 --> 00:49.382
ITO - THANKS FOR TODAY.
MR. SAKUMOTO REALLY ENJOYED IT!

00:50.425 --> 00:51.968
ALSO, I FORGOT TO TELL YOU,

00:52.051 --> 00:54.512
BUT I MET
MIYAUCHI AT A WEDDING THE OTHER DAY.

00:54.596 --> 00:56.264
SHE'S SO CUTE, AS ALWAYS.

00:59.809 --> 01:06.649
YOU USED TO DATE MIYAUCHI, RIGHT?

01:13.406 --> 01:14.240
CLOSED

01:14.324 --> 01:17.285
I'm glad your sister was all right.

01:17.368 --> 01:18.328
Me too.

01:18.411 --> 01:19.579
You were a lifesaver. Thanks.

01:19.662 --> 01:22.373
No worries.
It was just our regulars, anyway.

01:22.874 --> 01:26.127
I guess you can run this restaurant
without me now.

01:26.211 --> 01:28.004
No, no, I can't.

01:28.087 --> 01:29.547
I was panicking.

01:34.469 --> 01:35.970
- Shige…
- Huh?

01:36.721 --> 01:39.808
Thank you for the other day.

01:42.227 --> 01:45.522
I appreciate you taking me to the market.

01:46.105 --> 01:48.149
It cheered me up.

01:48.233 --> 01:49.275
Yeah?

01:50.568 --> 01:52.237
Well, I'll ask for your help again.

01:52.821 --> 01:53.655
- Of course.
- Okay.

01:55.323 --> 01:56.157
I'll get it.

01:58.535 --> 01:59.869
Hello, this is Tanomi.

01:59.953 --> 02:03.206
I'm very sorry this is so sudden.

02:04.541 --> 02:05.708
Thank you very much.

02:05.792 --> 02:08.253
Then I will visit before you open.

02:08.336 --> 02:10.046
Thank you very much.

02:11.256 --> 02:14.175
Miyauchi, are you open tomorrow at 17:00?

02:14.259 --> 02:15.969
I have one appointment.

02:16.052 --> 02:18.429
I'm going to propose the idea
for the reception.

02:19.347 --> 02:21.307
I might not make it in time.

02:21.391 --> 02:22.475
Okay.

02:22.559 --> 02:24.561
I'll give them an overview
while we're waiting.

02:25.603 --> 02:26.896
What's the place called?

02:27.564 --> 02:29.732
Tanomi. I sent you a link.

02:31.317 --> 02:34.362
All right.
I'll head there as soon as I'm done.

02:35.905 --> 02:39.117
I took a look at your revised file.

02:39.200 --> 02:43.454
Separately,
each piece looks somewhat passable.

02:44.038 --> 02:47.000
But as a whole,
it seemed incohesive to me.

02:48.543 --> 02:49.919
Incohesive?

02:50.962 --> 02:54.173
Can it be that you don't have
a clear picture of the general theme?

02:54.257 --> 02:58.177
What is the message
you want to convey through this piece?

03:01.180 --> 03:02.265
RISING BUBBLES,
BUBBLES DISAPPEAR INTO UNDERWATER WORLD

03:02.348 --> 03:03.600
UMEBOSHI CORALS SWAYING IN THE CURRENT

03:03.683 --> 03:07.437
The cultural festival is your chance
to promote your work before you graduate.

03:07.937 --> 03:09.606
So try to work on it a little bit more.

03:11.274 --> 03:14.152
Okay. I'll think about it.

03:30.168 --> 03:30.877
OVERVIEW OF RECEPTION FOR CLIENTS

03:30.960 --> 03:32.337
We're holding a reception

03:32.420 --> 03:35.882
for our authors
and those we want to show appreciation to.

03:35.965 --> 03:39.594
I believe our guests
would be thrilled if we could

03:39.677 --> 03:41.554
cater from your restaurant and serve

03:41.638 --> 03:44.599
the delicious food
that I always eat at Tanomi.

03:44.682 --> 03:45.683
I see…

03:46.351 --> 03:47.852
I appreciate it.

03:48.353 --> 03:51.064
It's an honor coming from you, Ms. Ishida.

03:51.147 --> 03:54.400
But we don't have
any experience in catering.

03:54.901 --> 03:59.239
Plus, this is our regular working day.

04:00.406 --> 04:02.992
Taiga, what do you think about this?

04:03.076 --> 04:04.077
Huh?

04:05.912 --> 04:07.914
I have done something like a soup kitchen

04:07.997 --> 04:10.541
when I went to training camp for my club.

04:11.251 --> 04:15.088
If we prepare for it well,
I don't think it will be impossible.

04:18.591 --> 04:20.635
All right then, Ms. Ishida.

04:21.469 --> 04:24.681
This is Hase, by the way.
How about we put him in charge?

04:25.556 --> 04:27.850
Of course, I will oversee it with him too.

04:28.351 --> 04:29.185
That's perfect.

04:29.269 --> 04:31.771
Okay, it's settled then.
Is that okay, Taiga?

04:32.981 --> 04:35.149
Yes. I look forward to working with you.

04:35.233 --> 04:36.526
Thank you!

04:36.609 --> 04:37.986
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

04:38.611 --> 04:41.030
I'm sorry I'm late.

04:43.574 --> 04:45.618
This is Miyauchi,
the one in charge of this event.

04:45.702 --> 04:46.536
Okay.

04:50.206 --> 04:51.291
Taiga?

04:52.417 --> 04:54.377
- What?
- You know each other?

04:54.961 --> 04:57.005
Oh, we went to college together.

04:57.088 --> 04:58.339
Oh yeah?

04:59.465 --> 05:00.967
Excuse me.

05:02.010 --> 05:04.512
- My name is Miyauchi Masumi.
- Hello.

05:05.221 --> 05:06.931
We will be in your care.

05:07.015 --> 05:09.350
I look forward to working with you.

05:09.434 --> 05:12.186
Well then, that makes things easier.

05:12.270 --> 05:13.313
- True.
- Hello.

05:13.396 --> 05:14.439
- Yeah.
- Hello.

05:14.522 --> 05:16.024
We'll be in your care.

06:24.300 --> 06:26.385
A publishing company's party, huh?

06:26.969 --> 06:28.304
That sounds cool.

06:28.387 --> 06:29.430
Thanks.

06:30.181 --> 06:31.682
She's our regular customer,

06:31.766 --> 06:34.685
and Shige said
that he'll leave it up to me,

06:34.769 --> 06:36.437
so I want to give it my all.

06:37.230 --> 06:38.397
I see.

06:38.898 --> 06:40.983
It might be a lot of work,
but do your best.

06:41.901 --> 06:43.111
Thanks.

06:44.112 --> 06:45.822
About the menu…

06:46.322 --> 06:47.949
Aside from the light refreshments,

06:48.032 --> 06:50.743
I'm thinking about serving
a nutritious, warm soup.

06:52.328 --> 06:54.831
What about dak gomtang?

06:55.915 --> 06:56.999
Dak gomtang?

07:02.672 --> 07:05.049
This might be easy to eat.

07:05.675 --> 07:06.676
Interesting…

07:06.759 --> 07:09.595
ENERGIZE YOURSELF
WITH THE CHICKEN SOUP - DAK GOMTANG

07:09.679 --> 07:11.681
RECIPE - TWO TO THREE SERVINGS

07:11.764 --> 07:13.516
This is great.

07:13.599 --> 07:15.143
Thank you, Rin.

07:15.643 --> 07:17.186
I need to work hard too.

07:23.651 --> 07:26.654
Are you working on your piece
for the cultural festival?

07:27.447 --> 07:28.781
Yeah.

07:28.865 --> 07:31.951
But I'm kind of having
a difficult time with it.

07:32.452 --> 07:33.703
I see…

07:34.579 --> 07:37.081
I wish I could do something to help.

07:37.582 --> 07:38.458
SALMON FILLETS PEEK OUT

07:38.541 --> 07:39.792
I'm hungry.

07:41.836 --> 07:43.504
Baegopa?

07:46.966 --> 07:48.718
I'm hungry.

07:52.263 --> 07:53.389
That's it.

07:54.515 --> 07:56.225
Something I can do for you.

08:02.023 --> 08:03.024
Onigiri.

08:04.442 --> 08:05.401
Yay!

08:08.321 --> 08:10.156
Let me see…

08:15.578 --> 08:20.041
A lot of people are going to be there
at your cultural festival, right?

08:20.124 --> 08:21.042
Yeah.

08:21.751 --> 08:24.462
I guess professional artists
are going to be there too.

08:24.962 --> 08:28.633
Apparently, the cultural festival has
opened up opportunities for many people.

08:29.467 --> 08:30.760
I see.

08:32.220 --> 08:35.473
So in order to achieve
some kind of success before graduation,

08:35.556 --> 08:38.142
this piece I'm working on
is really important.

08:39.894 --> 08:41.187
Graduation…

08:55.993 --> 08:59.413
I'm sure you'll be able to find
the answer you're looking for.

09:02.667 --> 09:03.751
Yeah…

09:08.798 --> 09:10.675
Okay, it's ready.

09:19.684 --> 09:21.143
Thank you for the food.

09:21.227 --> 09:22.186
Enjoy.

09:25.064 --> 09:27.608
It's warm. It's so comforting.

09:36.784 --> 09:38.911
If I find a job in Japan,

09:38.995 --> 09:41.330
I might be able to be with you longer.

09:44.875 --> 09:45.876
What?

09:47.670 --> 09:48.629
What?

09:51.757 --> 09:54.677
Forget what I said.
Oh, that reminds me. The flyer!

09:55.177 --> 09:56.387
The flyer…

09:56.887 --> 09:57.763
There it is.

09:58.389 --> 10:00.725
Can you post this at your restaurant?

10:01.225 --> 10:02.059
Okay.

10:04.103 --> 10:04.812
TOKYO UNIVERSITY OF FINE ARTS FESTIVAL

10:04.895 --> 10:06.272
It's the same…

10:07.565 --> 10:11.193
It's on the same day
as the event that I just told you about.

10:12.403 --> 10:13.613
Oh…

10:15.031 --> 10:18.284
Well, I guess
there's nothing we can do about that.

10:20.077 --> 10:23.247
When it's complete,
show me your artwork, okay?

10:24.749 --> 10:25.666
Okay.

11:09.710 --> 11:12.213
Oh my god!

11:12.296 --> 11:14.799
I'm only 10% finished.

11:15.591 --> 11:18.803
I just decided on my motif too.

11:19.678 --> 11:22.431
You still have time. No need to rush.

11:22.932 --> 11:26.227
Amane, you're already done, aren't you?

11:26.310 --> 11:27.311
Yeah.

11:27.978 --> 11:29.271
So fast…

11:30.064 --> 11:32.775
So, what are you doing after you graduate?

11:34.068 --> 11:37.613
I got a couple of offers,
but I'm still deciding.

11:37.696 --> 11:39.907
Mitsuki, you're going into gaming?

11:39.990 --> 11:42.701
The job offer will be revoked
if I can't graduate, though.

11:45.579 --> 11:47.706
Rin, you're going back to Korea, right?

11:48.541 --> 11:51.836
Actually, I haven't really decided yet.

11:52.420 --> 11:53.254
Really?

11:53.838 --> 11:58.634
I wonder if it's too late
to find a way to stay in Japan?

11:59.593 --> 12:03.055
Try going to Career Services.
You can get a consultation.

12:04.390 --> 12:06.392
- Thanks. I'll try going.
- Yeah.

12:08.978 --> 12:12.857
In your case,
it will be important to find a company

12:12.940 --> 12:15.359
that will support your visa application.

12:15.443 --> 12:18.487
Are there any job listings
for animation companies?

12:18.571 --> 12:20.489
Check that bulletin board over there.

12:21.365 --> 12:24.118
Those are all listings
catering to international students.

12:24.201 --> 12:25.953
JOB LISTINGS FOR INTERNATIONAL STUDENTS

12:38.215 --> 12:41.719
JOB OPENING

12:42.845 --> 12:45.347
Are you proposing
to Onigiri Man or something?

12:45.431 --> 12:48.934
No, I'm not. Where did that come from?

12:49.018 --> 12:52.897
Why are you looking for a job in Japan?

12:52.980 --> 12:54.899
Because you want to be with him, right?

12:55.649 --> 12:59.028
Or what? Do you seriously
just want to work over there?

13:01.155 --> 13:02.448
Well…

13:03.574 --> 13:06.243
At this rate,
I'll end up listening to my mom

13:06.327 --> 13:08.621
and giving up on my dream.

13:10.206 --> 13:11.999
Let me ask you this.

13:12.917 --> 13:14.835
What is the most important to you?

13:14.919 --> 13:16.253
Animation?

13:16.337 --> 13:17.463
Onigiri Man?

13:17.546 --> 13:19.048
Your mom?

13:19.131 --> 13:21.342
I can't answer that so suddenly…

13:25.387 --> 13:28.557
I don't know. They're all important.

13:31.018 --> 13:34.063
Sorry. I have to attend a meeting now.
Talk to you later.

13:34.146 --> 13:34.980
LEE YUNGYEOL EXITED THE ROOM

13:35.064 --> 13:35.981
Hey, wait…

13:47.159 --> 13:52.498
RÉSUMÉ

13:57.878 --> 14:02.049
It's nice and colorful,
and each bite leaves you satisfied.

14:02.758 --> 14:04.093
Thank you.

14:05.010 --> 14:06.262
This daikon can use

14:07.429 --> 14:09.890
a little more salt
if you want it to stay fresh longer.

14:10.891 --> 14:12.268
Okay.

14:12.351 --> 14:15.062
All right, that is all the input I have.

14:16.105 --> 14:18.440
Can I use the kitchen a little bit longer?

14:18.524 --> 14:20.234
Sure, but don't wear yourself out.

14:20.860 --> 14:23.654
I have to go too.
What about you, Miyauchi?

14:24.446 --> 14:27.408
I want to go over the logistics with him.

14:28.075 --> 14:29.201
Well then, goodbye.

14:29.285 --> 14:31.036
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye.

14:32.580 --> 14:35.583
First of all, let's talk about the venue.

14:36.417 --> 14:37.543
Okay.

14:42.798 --> 14:44.758
Okay, this is too awkward.

14:47.386 --> 14:48.554
I agree.

14:48.637 --> 14:50.806
Who would have thought I'd meet you here?

14:50.890 --> 14:52.725
- What a surprise.
- Yeah.

14:53.809 --> 14:55.978
Well, since this is for work,

14:56.061 --> 14:58.689
let's not walk on eggshells
around each other.

14:59.481 --> 15:01.358
- Okay. Thanks.
- Okay.

15:02.067 --> 15:04.945
So about the layout
for the day of the event…

15:05.029 --> 15:05.863
‪Yeah?

15:06.572 --> 15:09.450
I'm thinking of putting a table here
where you can cook.

15:11.952 --> 15:13.871
- This is just a suggestion, but…
- Yeah?

15:14.538 --> 15:16.498
Is there space for a portable stove?

15:17.958 --> 15:19.335
All right.

15:20.377 --> 15:21.503
What do you think?

15:31.347 --> 15:34.433
What in the world… This is great.

15:36.894 --> 15:38.687
Wow, thanks.

15:40.397 --> 15:41.523
Want to eat lunch?

15:42.399 --> 15:43.275
Yeah.

15:43.359 --> 15:45.736
Japanese sake…

15:46.612 --> 15:48.405
Oh, where's Taiga today?

15:48.489 --> 15:51.367
What?
Oh, I had him pick things up at the store.

15:53.035 --> 15:53.869
That reminds me.

15:53.953 --> 15:58.290
- He told me to give this to you, Noa.
- Huh?

15:58.374 --> 15:59.375
TOKYO UNIVERSITY OF FINE ARTS FESTIVAL

15:59.458 --> 16:00.334
What's this?

16:00.417 --> 16:02.920
Rin's school is having
a cultural festival, apparently.

16:03.003 --> 16:06.298
Now he's even advertising for her, huh?

16:06.382 --> 16:08.217
KAPPABASHI DOUGUGAI STREET

16:23.649 --> 16:25.567
Wow…

16:27.361 --> 16:28.404
There it is.

16:36.662 --> 16:37.705
What's this?

16:45.004 --> 16:46.672
How are you, Rin?

16:50.384 --> 16:53.345
Who is that old man? Where are you?

16:53.429 --> 16:54.930
Kappabashi.

16:55.014 --> 16:58.767
It's a place where they sell
a bunch of kitchenware and tableware.

16:58.851 --> 17:01.020
It's my first time coming here.

17:02.813 --> 17:04.940
There's something similar in Korea.

17:05.024 --> 17:07.693
It's called Hwanghak-dong.

17:08.193 --> 17:10.779
They sell frying pans
and glassware and stuff.

17:10.863 --> 17:12.906
Oh yeah? Hwanghak-dong?

17:14.450 --> 17:16.702
If you're ever there, show it to me.

17:17.411 --> 17:18.829
Show you Hwanghak-dong?

17:20.581 --> 17:21.582
Sure.

17:26.086 --> 17:29.423
No matter where you go,

17:30.340 --> 17:34.178
let's share what we're seeing,
just like we are now, and go on dates.

17:36.346 --> 17:37.222
What?

17:38.057 --> 17:41.477
There's no time difference,
so we can talk to each other anytime.

17:45.481 --> 17:49.818
If both of us try our best,
even if we're far apart,

17:50.319 --> 17:52.404
I don't think we'll be lonely.

17:52.488 --> 17:53.906
- I know, right?
- Yeah!

17:53.989 --> 17:56.533
- I'm wearing print on print.
- That's too much!

17:56.617 --> 18:00.037
Sorry, you have class, huh?
I'll call you tonight.

18:00.120 --> 18:01.371
Okay.

18:08.879 --> 18:11.465
You don't care if we're far apart, do you?

18:18.180 --> 18:21.892
JUN-HO - DID YOU EAT ALREADY?

18:23.852 --> 18:25.187
"No matter where I go"?

18:26.188 --> 18:28.482
Why is he assuming that I'm going away?

18:29.983 --> 18:31.276
You're an international student…

18:32.528 --> 18:37.116
I know, but doesn't he want to be with me?

18:38.867 --> 18:42.621
He can't just tell you to stay in Japan.
That would be irresponsible.

18:45.374 --> 18:48.877
I'm not talking about responsibility.

18:48.961 --> 18:52.005
I just want to know how Taiga truly feels.

19:00.305 --> 19:04.351
I know.
Taiga is an honest and sincere guy.

19:05.310 --> 19:09.273
He's not the type
to thoughtlessly say things like that.

19:10.566 --> 19:12.317
But still…

19:15.779 --> 19:16.822
Rin.

19:18.490 --> 19:22.035
Right now, the most important thing
is to think about what you want

19:22.119 --> 19:23.704
to do with your future, right?

19:23.787 --> 19:25.289
You can think about him after that.

19:30.043 --> 19:31.920
You came to Japan
to study animation, right?

19:34.631 --> 19:35.465
‪Right…

19:39.428 --> 19:40.929
Well then, do your best.

19:41.471 --> 19:44.433
I'm looking forward
to your cultural festival, too.

19:45.142 --> 19:47.311
For now, focus on your artwork.

19:49.062 --> 19:50.189
Okay?

19:52.482 --> 19:53.692
You're right.

19:55.194 --> 19:57.863
I should be focusing
on what's in front of me first.

20:01.074 --> 20:04.369
Master, I am deeply grateful.

20:07.289 --> 20:08.415
Is that so?

20:08.498 --> 20:10.626
Should you need more assistance,
you may ask me.

20:33.565 --> 20:35.400
- Taiga.
- Huh?

20:37.611 --> 20:40.197
The cooking space
that I was talking about…

20:46.370 --> 20:47.746
10 MINUTES - GAMEY

20:47.829 --> 20:49.831
20 MINUTES - NOT GAMEY - NOT ENOUGH COLOR

20:49.915 --> 20:51.833
30 MINUTES

21:12.813 --> 21:16.858
UPLOAD COMPLETE

21:31.206 --> 21:33.625
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

21:33.709 --> 21:35.669
- Hello.
- Hello.

21:35.752 --> 21:38.505
- Here you go.
- We have postcards here.

21:38.588 --> 21:40.674
- Please take a look.
- Enjoy.

21:58.483 --> 22:03.030
TAIGA - I'M SORRY I CAN'T GO TODAY
I CAN'T WAIT TO SEE YOU TONIGHT

22:16.209 --> 22:17.336
Mr. Hase.

22:17.836 --> 22:20.130
It's almost time.

22:20.213 --> 22:21.673
We'll be in your care.

22:22.716 --> 22:23.842
Yes.

22:24.760 --> 22:29.556
RECEPTION - MEIYOSHA

22:32.476 --> 22:33.852
Noa, you're off work?

22:34.603 --> 22:36.813
Yes, I forgot to add another shift.

22:43.862 --> 22:46.281
HOW IS IT GOING TODAY?

22:46.364 --> 22:51.369
AKINORI - IN LINE AT THE PACHINKO PARLOR
MIGHT NEED YOU LATER

23:00.003 --> 23:01.838
TOKYO UNIVERSITY OF FINE ARTS FESTIVAL

23:01.922 --> 23:05.717
I redrew the moment
the character falls, over and over again,

23:05.801 --> 23:08.553
and adjusted the timing
until the very last minute.

23:08.637 --> 23:11.181
So when I heard the audience laugh,
I felt very happy.

23:11.264 --> 23:13.892
Your experimentation with the timing
really paid off.

23:15.435 --> 23:18.897
Well then, please give her
another round of applause.

23:26.696 --> 23:29.449
Next up, is Ms. Park Rin.

23:33.537 --> 23:34.871
You can do it, Rin!

23:46.299 --> 23:49.427
I am Park Rin, a second-year
in the Department of Animation.

23:50.011 --> 23:52.639
The title is Onigiri.

23:53.140 --> 23:55.016
I hope you enjoy it.

23:55.892 --> 23:57.727
Thank you for watching.

24:10.365 --> 24:12.826
TOKYO UNIVERSITY OF FINE ARTS
DEPARTMENT OF ANIMATION

24:12.909 --> 24:15.829
ONIGIRI - PARK RIN

25:33.281 --> 25:34.991
Where do you want to go?

25:35.075 --> 25:36.785
I want to go see

25:36.868 --> 25:38.787
- that pretty blue artwork.
- Me too.

25:49.923 --> 25:52.342
ONIGIRI

25:52.425 --> 25:53.551
Noa?

25:57.514 --> 25:58.348
Hello.

25:59.474 --> 26:01.059
I didn't know you came.

26:02.143 --> 26:05.063
I got a flyer at Tanomi.

26:05.146 --> 26:06.481
And I had time, so…

26:08.024 --> 26:09.442
What did you think?

26:12.612 --> 26:17.701
Well, it's so different from
the world that I live in.

26:17.784 --> 26:19.536
So it was new and exciting.

26:24.624 --> 26:25.750
Is she your friend?

26:28.128 --> 26:31.047
She's Noa,
a regular at Taiga's restaurant.

26:32.382 --> 26:33.633
Hello.

26:34.426 --> 26:35.635
I'm Rin's senior from college.

26:36.219 --> 26:37.387
Kang Jun-ho.

26:40.849 --> 26:43.810
We have to celebrate tonight,
since you worked so hard.

26:45.020 --> 26:46.563
Want to come too, Noa?

26:47.230 --> 26:49.524
No, it's okay. I have to go to work.

26:51.568 --> 26:52.902
I'm sorry.

26:52.986 --> 26:55.322
I promised to meet Taiga today.

26:56.114 --> 26:57.282
Promised?

26:58.116 --> 27:00.118
We're going to have
an afterparty together.

27:03.663 --> 27:06.499
I see. Another time, then.

27:08.209 --> 27:09.461
Thank you.

27:09.544 --> 27:10.795
- Thank you.
- Hello.

27:10.879 --> 27:12.422
Thank you.

27:14.215 --> 27:15.550
Hello.

27:27.562 --> 27:30.982
- Even the background is calculated.
- What artists have inspired you?

27:31.066 --> 27:32.942
I wasn't inspired by anyone.

27:33.026 --> 27:35.403
I imagined everything in my mind.

27:35.487 --> 27:37.113
- Of course.
- Amazing.

27:37.197 --> 27:39.491
I bet all the studios want you.

27:39.574 --> 27:41.868
I've never seen a student
with this much talent.

27:41.951 --> 27:43.495
- I agree.
- True.

27:44.621 --> 27:45.872
She's amazing.

27:46.831 --> 27:48.208
Ms. Park Rin?

27:49.834 --> 27:50.710
Yes?

27:50.794 --> 27:53.880
I saw your film.

27:53.963 --> 27:55.465
It was very interesting.

27:58.343 --> 27:59.886
Thank you very much.

27:59.969 --> 28:03.890
You have a very unique perspective.

28:03.973 --> 28:07.602
Also, the characters were very cute.

28:09.896 --> 28:11.856
You like Onigiri?

28:12.440 --> 28:14.776
Yes, I do.

28:15.693 --> 28:16.694
I see.

28:18.571 --> 28:23.535
I've posted my past works
on my social media.

28:23.618 --> 28:24.536
If you'd like…

28:24.619 --> 28:26.496
Thank you. I'll take a look at them.

28:35.630 --> 28:36.798
Thank you.

28:45.098 --> 28:46.057
Here you go.

28:49.602 --> 28:50.854
This is so good.

28:50.937 --> 28:53.356
Soup really hits the spot
at these kinds of events.

28:54.524 --> 28:57.485
It's such a comforting and warm flavor.

28:59.863 --> 29:02.240
- I came back for seconds.
- Thank you.

29:03.408 --> 29:04.951
This is really good.

29:05.034 --> 29:06.161
Yes.

29:06.244 --> 29:08.163
- It's called dak gomtang.
- Oh I see.

29:11.040 --> 29:13.668
- Want to sing together?
- Really? I'd love that!

29:13.752 --> 29:14.878
I'd love that!

29:17.213 --> 29:18.131
Here you go.

29:22.385 --> 29:26.806
Jun-ho, are you Rin's ex-boyfriend
or something?

29:30.602 --> 29:31.478
Of course not!

29:32.854 --> 29:36.816
If I was her ex,
I would never go to see her like that.

29:36.900 --> 29:40.069
Really? What's the big deal?

29:40.153 --> 29:41.654
It's unacceptable

29:42.197 --> 29:45.950
to hang out with your ex
when you're dating someone new.

29:46.826 --> 29:48.703
Interesting…

29:48.787 --> 29:50.246
You're pretty strict, huh?

29:50.330 --> 29:54.250
When you're dating,
trust is everything, after all.

29:56.085 --> 29:58.171
Trust, huh?

30:00.423 --> 30:02.008
Noa…

30:02.091 --> 30:06.137
Why aren't you checking your phone?
I was on a roll today, you know?

30:06.221 --> 30:07.305
Sorry.

30:08.097 --> 30:09.307
Water, please.

30:13.269 --> 30:14.604
What's wrong?

30:14.687 --> 30:16.815
Were you dumped by a girl or something?

30:18.441 --> 30:20.026
- Here.
- Thanks.

30:20.109 --> 30:21.069
Oh?

30:23.029 --> 30:24.531
You're the one from the other day…

30:29.452 --> 30:30.286
You know each other?

30:30.370 --> 30:32.372
Cheers!

30:38.127 --> 30:39.337
That's good.

30:39.420 --> 30:40.964
I see.

30:41.047 --> 30:44.342
So hyeongnim means older brother?

30:45.385 --> 30:48.179
Even if it's not your real brother,
you can use it for good friends.

30:48.263 --> 30:49.722
Interesting.

30:50.306 --> 30:52.725
I love that.

30:53.434 --> 30:55.687
I'm an only child, after all.

30:56.187 --> 30:59.190
If only I had an older brother like you…

31:00.149 --> 31:00.984
I can only wish.

31:04.320 --> 31:05.613
What are you saying?

31:05.697 --> 31:07.782
We had drinks together,
so we're basically brothers.

31:09.284 --> 31:12.370
Hyeongnim! I'll be in your care!

31:13.746 --> 31:16.082
I'm happy to have
a dongsaeng in Japan now.

31:18.042 --> 31:20.003
- Hyeongnim!
- Dongsaeng!

31:29.095 --> 31:31.055
- Did you really--
- So good!

31:32.473 --> 31:34.559
Your cooking is the best!

31:35.143 --> 31:36.227
It was so delicious!

31:37.520 --> 31:38.646
Thank you.

31:39.731 --> 31:42.817
The party was a success, huh?
That's great.

31:45.069 --> 31:49.282
There's a lot I need to improve on,
but I felt a strong sense of fulfillment.

31:50.199 --> 31:52.035
What does "fulfillment" mean again?

31:53.077 --> 31:54.078
Um…

31:55.163 --> 31:57.248
Like a feeling of accomplishment.

31:57.999 --> 32:02.420
The excitement you feel when you
succeed in doing what you needed to do.

32:07.342 --> 32:10.094
Rin, you're the amazing one.
I can't believe you made this.

32:14.098 --> 32:17.435
My classmate was getting
a lot more recognition.

32:18.645 --> 32:19.771
But…

32:21.439 --> 32:24.108
I put in everything
that I could right now.

32:26.361 --> 32:27.528
That's why…

32:28.529 --> 32:30.949
I will pat myself on the back for now.

32:32.909 --> 32:34.619
- That's right.
- Yup.

32:41.250 --> 32:42.961
I thought about it…

32:44.170 --> 32:45.964
Just like you said,

32:46.923 --> 32:50.843
if we try our best to share
everything with each other,

32:52.387 --> 32:56.766
we won't be lonely
even if we're far apart…

32:58.017 --> 32:59.477
I think.

33:12.907 --> 33:14.409
Yeah…

33:16.577 --> 33:17.453
Let's try our best.

33:25.628 --> 33:26.838
Rin…

33:27.922 --> 33:32.343
One thing on your bucket list was
"drinking ramune at a hot spring," right?

33:33.594 --> 33:34.804
Yeah.

33:37.640 --> 33:42.145
Now that we're finally not so busy,
why don't we celebrate

33:42.228 --> 33:43.855
and go on a trip?

33:44.522 --> 33:46.983
Let's drink ramune at a hot spring.

33:52.822 --> 33:54.115
I'd love that.

34:15.970 --> 34:19.098
Mr. Hase's food was a great hit!

34:19.182 --> 34:21.017
- We need to work together again.
- Yes.

34:21.768 --> 34:23.478
- Right?
- All right, let's drink tonight.

34:24.645 --> 34:25.688
Oh, that reminds me.

34:25.772 --> 34:30.651
A customer gave me
some good sake, so I chilled it.

34:30.735 --> 34:32.528
Hey, Master.

34:32.612 --> 34:35.031
Why are you trying to get me drunk?

34:35.615 --> 34:38.451
Reiko, let's give this back to them.

34:39.118 --> 34:40.870
Tanukichi!

34:41.871 --> 34:44.749
- Let's go home.
- I'm going home.

34:44.832 --> 34:46.751
- Take me.
- Thank you very much.

34:46.834 --> 34:49.128
- Thank you.
- Thank you. Get home safe.

34:55.384 --> 34:57.929
TANOMI

34:58.012 --> 34:59.430
Up we go.

35:02.183 --> 35:03.184
Good work.

35:07.647 --> 35:09.232
Masumi?

35:12.026 --> 35:13.236
My answer?

35:15.822 --> 35:16.948
The art instructor position?

35:17.031 --> 35:18.241
Yes.

35:18.324 --> 35:21.953
It'll be rude to make them
wait any longer.

35:22.036 --> 35:26.124
And plus,
you have no other options, right?

35:26.207 --> 35:27.416
That's not…

35:27.500 --> 35:28.251
‪NUMAZU PORT, UCHIURA PORT
‪LOCAL FISH THAT'S IN SEASON

35:28.334 --> 35:30.962
Please just give me a little more time.

35:39.095 --> 35:40.263
TO: STUDIO JUPITET
RÉSUMÉ INCLUDED

35:54.610 --> 35:56.112
I sent it.

36:13.671 --> 36:15.840
You don't have to be so on guard.

36:17.383 --> 36:20.636
But I guess, who wouldn't be,
if your ex-girlfriend ambushes you?

36:21.512 --> 36:22.930
That's not it…

36:25.600 --> 36:29.145
I wanted to apologize to you.

36:30.104 --> 36:32.607
For saying a lot
of condescending stuff to you back then.

36:33.774 --> 36:35.359
I'm really sorry.

36:35.443 --> 36:36.861
Wait, wait, what?

36:37.904 --> 36:41.782
Back then, as in when we were dating?

36:42.825 --> 36:43.826
Yeah.

36:45.453 --> 36:47.205
That was…

36:48.122 --> 36:50.374
my fault for dwelling on the past.

36:51.209 --> 36:52.460
That's not true.

36:53.169 --> 36:55.087
I was overwhelmed myself.

36:56.214 --> 37:00.051
I had just started working
and all I could think about

37:00.134 --> 37:04.263
was my future and "planning my life."

37:08.392 --> 37:09.560
But right now,

37:10.394 --> 37:14.357
I kind of understand how you felt.

37:16.567 --> 37:17.735
What?

37:19.779 --> 37:23.491
The thing is, I'm dating a girl right now.

37:24.408 --> 37:26.202
She's from Korea.

37:29.121 --> 37:30.248
Oh yeah?

37:33.542 --> 37:36.921
She's planning on returning home
in a few months,

37:38.297 --> 37:39.507
but…

37:40.216 --> 37:42.760
Sometimes I wonder if
I would be able to tell her

37:43.886 --> 37:46.764
something different
if I had a clearer vision of my future.

37:52.061 --> 37:56.399
But I guess I just have to do my best,
one thing at a time.

38:03.781 --> 38:06.617
Taiga, you've changed.

38:15.584 --> 38:16.419
‪How?

38:17.837 --> 38:18.671
You look old.

38:20.381 --> 38:21.507
‪Come on…

38:21.590 --> 38:24.552
- That goes for you too.
- Not at all.

38:33.686 --> 38:37.148
Why wouldn't you turn down
a job offer from your ex-girlfriend?

38:37.231 --> 38:39.775
I wish you would've accepted it,
even just for a second.

38:39.859 --> 38:42.945
Sorry. I can't keep up with you.

38:43.029 --> 38:43.904
Subtitle translation by: Kiko Morita
